G3650.def:
**ὅλος**, -η, -ον,
[in LXX chiefly for כֹּל ;]
**of persons and things, whole, entire, complete**;
1. of indefinite ideas, with subst. anarth.: [[Luk.5.5|Luk.5:5]], [[Act.11.26; 28.30|Act.11:26 28:30]], [[Tit.1.11|Tit.1:11]]; ὅλον ἄνθρωπον (**an entire man**; see Field, _Notes_, 93), [[Jhn.7.23|Jhn.7:23]] ὅλη Ἰερουσαλήμ (= πᾶσα Ἰ, [[Mat.2.3|Mat.2:3]] see Bl., §47, 9), [[Act.21.31|Act.21:31]]
2. Definite, with art.;
(a) preceding subst.: [[Mat.4.23, 24|Mat.4:23, 24]] [[Luk.8.39|Luk.8:39]], [[1Co.12.17|1Co.12:17]], al.;
(b) following subst.: [[Mrk.1.33|Mrk.1:33]], [[Luk.9.25|Luk.9:25]], [[Jhn.4.53|Jhn.4:53]], [[Act.21.30|Act.21:30]], al.;
(with) between art. and subst., where subst. is an abstract noun (Plat., al.).
3. Attached to adj. or verb: [[Mat.13.33|Mat.13:33]], [[Luk.13.21|Luk.13:21]], [[Jhn.9.34|Jhn.9:34]], al.; adverbially, δι ̓ ὅλου (MM, xviii), [[Jhn.19.23|Jhn.19:23]]
(AS)

G3625.def:
**οἰκουμένη**, -ης, ἡ
(fern. Pres. pass. ptcp. of οἰκέω; sc. γῆ) [in LXX chiefly for תֵּבֵל, אֶרֶץ ;]
**the inhabited earth**;
(a) in cl., the countries occupied by Greeks, as disting. from barbarian lands (Hdt., Dem., al.);
(b) **in later writers, the Roman world**: [[Luk.2.1|Luk.2:1]], [[Act.11.28; 24.5|Act.11:28 24:5]]; by meton., of its inhabitants : [[Act.17.6; 19.27|Act.17:6 19:27]];
(with) in LXX ([[Psa.23.1; 71.8|Psa.23:1 71:8]], al.) and NT, also of the whole inhabited world: [[Mat.24.14|Mat.24:14]], [[Luk.4.5; 21.26|Luk.4:5 21:26]], [[Rom.10.18|Rom.10:18]], [[Heb.1.6|Heb.1:6]], [[Rev.3.10; 16.14|Rev.3:10 16:14]]; by meton. (ut supr.), [[Act.17.31|Act.17:31]], [[Rev.12.9|Rev.12:9]];
(d) of the Messianic age, ἡ οἰ. ἡ μέλλουσα = ὁ αἰὼ ὁ μέλλων: [[Heb.2.5|Heb.2:5]]†
(AS)

G3674.def:
**ὁμοῦ**
_ adv._ (ὁμός),
**together**;
(a) prop., of place: [[Jhn.21.2|Jhn.21:2]], [[Act.2.1|Act.2:1]];
(b) **without idea of place**: [[Jhn.4.36; 20.4|Jhn.4:36 20:4]].†
(AS)

G3667.def:
**ὁμοίωμα**, -τος, τό
(ὁμοιόω), [in LXX for דְּמוּת, תַּבְנִית, תְּמוּנָה, etc. ;]
**that which is made like something**;
(a) concrete, an image, like­ness ([[Psa.106.20|Psa.106:20]], [[Ezk.1.5|Eze.1:5]], [[1Ma.3.48|1Ma.3:48]], al.) : [[Rev.9.7|Rev.9:7]];
(b) **abstract, like­ness, resemblance**: [[Rom.5.14; 6.5; 8.3|Rom.5:14 6:5 8:3]], [[Php.2.7|Php.2:7]]; ἐν ὁ. εἰκόνος, [[Rom.1.23|Rom.1:23]]†
_SYN._: εἰκών (which see), ὁμοίωσις (AS)
